{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3MVgJMEzsQA8h3RcjYN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run test:ssr` and `npm test` pass\n\nThe server templater now escapes interpolated attribute values once and writes the same attributes as the browser for the same markup. A link whose query contains `&` is correct before any JavaScript runs. All five checklist items are done and committed. In the final runs `npm run test:ssr` passed 94/94, `npm test` passed 316/316, and lint is clean.\n\n**Why the last attempt failed:** its code was fine; the test gate died because port 8123 was already in use. The same thing happened once here. The port was free a moment later and a rerun passed, so it's probably a test run in another worktree using the same port. If the orchestrator runs worktrees in parallel, it can hit this again on the next gate, whatever the code does.\n\n**The fix, in `src/htm.ts`:**\n1. Values in attribute positions are unwrapped from the templater's escaping wrapper before being escaped. Before, they were escaped twice (`&` became `&amp;amp;`). This covers plain elements and non-declared attributes on a component.\n2. Non-declared attributes on a component now follow the browser's rules: `true` becomes an empty attribute, and `false`, `null` and `undefined` are left out. Before, they were written as the strings \"true\", \"false\" and \"null\".\n\n`src/builders.ts` needed no change, because it already writes an empty value as a bare attribute.\n\n**Tests:** the new `test/parity.ts` holds a single table of input and expected HTML. It covers `&`, quotes and `<` in plain and component attributes, function and number values, the four boolean and null values, a declared prop, and nested markup. `test/ssr.ts` checks the server output against it. `test/index.ts` checks the browser `String()` output against it, and also checks that server and browser give the same HTML once the server's markers are removed.\n\nI saw both sides fail first. The SSR suite failed on the double escaping and the \"true\"/\"false\" strings, and against the old `src/htm.ts` the browser suite's comparison failed 9 cases. The existing exact-string static page assertions in the SSR suite passed without changes.\n\n`stripMarkers` already removes the `<!--[c-->` children marker that a later ticket will add, so the table won't need editing then. I also added a short note on the parity table to `AGENTS.md`. My notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md` and are not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1177,"cache_read_input_tokens":70185,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1177},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"539ac82f-5d72-4286-99fe-af30bcce7238","uuid":"92eeb4c0-89ea-4b63-909c-2f341638dc98","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:59:57.319Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3MVg2UjMu8iyuQWaCzp"}
